Watch_Dogs 2 came with a variety of changes and improvements when compared to its predecessor:
- a more fluid parkour system: now you can climb, jump and move around faster;
- you can now customize your character with a layered system: hats, masks, tops, pants, shoes can now be equipped separately, unlike in Watch_Dogs, where complete outfits were used;
- AI is a lot better: the police will respond to crimes and even arrest NPCs that attack the player character;
- There is now a built-in option to downsample the pixel density, helping improve performance if you have a bottleneck, like in my case (which does not mean the game is not optimized);
- There is now a bigger vehicle variety;
- Hacking mechanics have returned and have been heavily extended: now you have an RC car, a drone and a greater number of gadgets at your disposal;
- A dynamic field-of-view effect was added, making it look at lot prettier;
- The color pallet is more varied, and because of this landscapes appear a lot more vibrant and cheerful to the eye;
- You can now interact in different ways with NPCs, such as talking to people and playing with dogs;
- The game came with a decent optimization level, specially considering it was a port from the PS4;
- It can and will be VERY demanding and resource-hungry due to employing latest technologies and advanced graphic effects, and for this reason it might not run so well in a gaming laptop of the actual generation;
- The multiplayer has been extended with co-op missions, and now there is a bigger focus on co-op than on pvp like in Watch_Dogs;
- Players will see each other while roaming around the game's world, and can even interact, and start missions on the fly, without any connection screen;
Of course there will be occasional bugs, like NPCs behaving weirdly, strange animations, but for now, there is no game breaking bug, not that I could find one yet, but I'll keep updating this review as I progress through the game.
That said, my personal verdict:
10/10, next to zero regret on the pre-order.

